[
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 31898,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 133,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Schematic representation of the serrated neoplasia pathway</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Sessile serrated lesions (SSLs) have <em>BRAF</em> mutation and can develop de novo or possibly (dotted line) from microvesicular hyperplastic polyps (HPs). A key molecular event thought to precipitate the progression of SSL to malignancy is either <em>MLH1</em> methylation, secondary to high levels of CpG island methylator phenotype (CIMP), progressing to mismatch repair (MMR)-deficient colorectal carcinoma, or <em>TP53</em> mutation progressing to MMR-proficient colorectal carcinoma. Traditional serrated adenomas (TSAs) may develop de&nbsp;novo, possibly from SSL or from goblet cell HP (dotted lines). TSAs progress via the <em>BRAF</em> or <em>KRAS</em> pathway to high-grade dysplasia and MMR-proficient colorectal carcinoma. WNT signalling pathway activation occurs in all pathways through different mechanisms, at the transition to dysplasia.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/133.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_133.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32020,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 337,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Goblet cell&ndash;rich hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>At low power, the crypts are wider and taller than normal.</p>",
    "source": "Rish K Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/337.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_337.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32021,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 338,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Goblet cell&ndash;rich hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>At high power, the crypts contain a large number of goblet cells with superficial serration.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Rish K Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/338.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_338.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32022,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 339,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Goblet cell&ndash;rich hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>A transition between normal colonic mucosa and the polyp is apparent in the right portion of the biopsy. Only subtle superficial serration is seen in this example.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/339.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_339.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32023,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 340,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>This lesion&nbsp;is characterized by many architecturally distorted serrated crypts.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/340.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_340.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32024,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 341,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Microvesicular hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The serrated crypts are narrow and architectural features of sessile serrated lesion are absent.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/341.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_341.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32025,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 342,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Microvesicular hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The crypts are straight and narrow, and they are lined by serrated epithelium.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/342.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_342.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32026,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 343,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Microvesicular hyperplastic polyp</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The surface epithelium shows typical serration and is composed of a mixture of microvesicular and goblet cells; the basement membrane area beneath the surface epithelium is thickened.</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/343.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_343.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32027,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 344,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Architecturally distorted serrated crypts with prominent basal crypt dilatation.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/344.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_344.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32028,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 345,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Architecturally distorted serrated crypts with deep crypt serrations and basal crypt dilatation with lateral growth along the muscularis mucosae.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/345.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_345.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32029,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 346,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Architecturally distorted serrated crypts with lateral growth along the muscularis mucosae.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/346.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_346.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32030,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 347,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Architecturally distorted serrated crypts with deep crypt serrations and lateral growth along the muscularis mucosae.</p>",
    "source": "Rish K Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/347.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_347.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32031,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 348,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>A small SSL characterized by a single architecturally distorted crypt, but other features of SSL are also present.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Rish K Pai",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/348.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_348.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32032,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 349,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>An SSL with mucosal herniation of serrated crypts into the submucosa.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/349.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_349.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32033,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 350,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The dysplastic component on the left is sharply demarcated from the SSL on the right and shows partial villous architecture.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/350.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_350.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32034,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 351,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>In the same lesion, there is nuclear pleomorphism, loss of nuclear polarity, mitotic figures, and amphophilic mucin-depleted cytoplasm.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/351.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_351.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32035,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 354,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The dysplastic cells have reduced mucin content with gastric foveolar differentiation.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/354.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_354.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32036,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 355,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>In this case, the dysplastic crypts exhibit complex architecture with serration, crypt branching, and focal cribriforming.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/355.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_355.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32037,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 356,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>At low power, the small flat area of dysplasia on the upper right is characterized by crypt crowding, reduced lamina propria, and eosinophilic cells.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/356.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_356.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32038,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 357,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>At higher power, the dysplastic area shows complete loss of MLH1 expression by immunohistochemistry.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/357.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_357.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32039,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 358,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>In contrast with the non-dysplastic crypt on the right, the dysplastic area is characterized by crypt crowding and subtle cytological changes.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/358.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_358.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32040,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 359,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Loss of MLH1 expression can help in the diagnosis of SSL with subtle dysplastic changes.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/359.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_359.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32041,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 360,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Traditional serrated adenoma (TSA)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>This protuberant TSA shows complex villiform projections and slit-like serration.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/360.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_360.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32042,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 361,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Traditional serrated adenoma (TSA)</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The cells lining the villi are predominantly tall and columnar, with abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm and centrally located oval nuclei with pseudostratification but no mitotic activity. Note the multiple ectopic crypt formations along the villi with differentiated goblet cells.</p>",
    "source": "Christophe Rosty",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/361.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_361.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32270,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 926,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Colorectal serrated lesions and polyps, endoscopic appearance</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Microvesicular hyperplastic polyp. A small polyp with well-defined margins and an open pit pattern.&nbsp;</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/926.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_926.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32271,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 927,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Colorectal serrated lesions and polyps, endoscopic appearance</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>This lesion is large and has poorly defined margins.</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/927.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_927.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32272,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 928,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Colorectal serrated lesions and polyps, endoscopic appearance</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Traditional serrated adenoma. A large lesion composed of a central, protruding polypoid mass with a coral-like appearance.</p>",
    "source": "Markus Makinen",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/928.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_928.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32837,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 5590,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Tangential sections often result in difficulties in the diagnosis of serrated lesions. Although irregularities in crypt shape and diameter are suggestive of a sessile serrated lesion, evaluation of deeper levels is warranted</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "Robert D. Odze",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/5590.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_5590.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32838,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 5591,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "<p>Sessile serrated lesion (SSL) with dysplasia</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>The serrated dysplastic epithelium shows an irregular serrated or sawtooth pattern of growth lined by cells with hyperchromatic enlarged and slightly stratified nuclei and eosinophilic cytoplasm, similar in appearance to a serrated adenoma.</p>",
    "source": "Robert D. Odze",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "",
    "imageUrl": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/5591.jpg",
    "thumbnail": "https://tumourclassification.iarc.who.int/static/dzi/31/57/thumb_5591.jpg"
  },
  {
    "pkattachmentId": 32925,
    "bookid": 31,
    "chapterId": 57,
    "fileId": 934,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;6.01</strong> Histological and molecular features of serrated polyps</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "source error",
    "copyright": "",
    "tablehtml": "<table border=\"1\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td rowspan=\"2\" width=\"61\">\r\n<p><strong>Type</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"626\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>Histological features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td colspan=\"3\" width=\"250\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>Molecular features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p><strong>Crypt architecture</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p><strong>Proliferation zone</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p><strong>Cytological features</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p><strong>Mucin type</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong><em>BRAF</em> mutation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong><em>KRAS</em> mutation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><strong>CpG-island methylation</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"61\">\r\n<p>MVHP</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p>Funnel-shaped crypts with serrations limited to upper two&nbsp;thirds</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p>Located uniformly in the basal portion of crypts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p>Small basally located nuclei; no dysplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p>Mixed microvesicular and goblet cell</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">70&ndash;80%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">0%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"61\">\r\n<p>GCHP</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p>Elongated crypts that resemble enlarged normal crypts; little to no serration</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p>Located uniformly in the basal portion of crypts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p>Small basally located nuclei; no dysplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p>Goblet cell predominant</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">0%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">50%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">&minus;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"61\">\r\n<p>SSL</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p>Horizontal growth along the muscularis mucosae, dilation of the crypt base (basal third of the crypt), and/or serrations extending into the crypt base</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p>Proliferation may be abnormally located away from the crypt base, variable from crypt to crypt</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p>Small basally located nuclei with occasional larger nuclei with inconspicuous nucleoli; no dysplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p>Mixed microvesicular and goblet cell</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">&gt;&nbsp;90%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">0%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">++</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"61\">\r\n<p>SSLD</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p>Complex architecture in the dysplastic component (crypt crowding, complex branching, cribriforming, villous architecture)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p>Like in SSL, but with more proliferation in the dysplastic component</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p>Varied morphological appearance of dysplastic component</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p>Varied type</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">&gt;&nbsp;90%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">0%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">+++</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td width=\"61\">\r\n<p>TSA</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"184\">\r\n<p>Slit-like serrations; often ectopic crypts</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"160\">\r\n<p>Present within ectopic crypts and crypt bases</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"151\">\r\n<p>Elongated pencillate nuclei with nuclear stratification and cytoplasmic eosinophilia; may develop overt dysplasia</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"131\">\r\n<p>Occasional scattered goblet cells; rare goblet cell subtype has been described</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">50&ndash;70%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"77\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">20&ndash;40%</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"96\">\r\n<p align=\"center\">+</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>GCHP, goblet cell&ndash;rich hyperplastic polyp; MVHP, microvesicular hyperplastic polyp; SSL, sessile serrated lesion; SSLD, sessile serrated lesion with dysplasia; TSA, traditional serrated adenoma.</p>",
    "imageUrl": null,
    "thumbnail": null
  }
]